      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "RED CODE (6) earns top billing after winning a Class 3 over 1000m at this track, beating Champonnet by half a length despite racing wide throughout and hanging in passing the 200m. He now reaches the third run of the campaign, is tagged for a class drop into this BM60, and his 1200m record is sound enough to keep the rise in trip in perspective. RICALLEN (7) is the main danger after sprinting clear to win well at this venue, with three wins from eight starts around 1200m reinforcing the strength of that last-start result. ALLEZIZZY (2) backed up consistent local form with a narrow win here, though she rises from picnic grade to harder company and was beaten by RICALLEN the run prior. SIR LUNCHALOTS (8) comes through strong form references and is drawn favourably. Keeping onside.",
